Extract one object per signoff person. If multiple people signed, create separate objects for each.

A "signoff person" is strictly defined as an individual who is executing, adopting, or authorizing the document itself. They are found in ONE OR MORE of these patterns:

PATTERN 1 - Traditional clause: Signature block under "IN WITNESS WHEREOF" or similar execution language.

PATTERN 2 - Location/date header block: A block where a city and date line (e.g., "Stuttgart im November 2025" or "Stuttgart in November 2025") is followed by a company name (e.g., "Mercedes-Benz Group AG"), then one or more handwritten signatures, each with a printed name and title below them. ALL individuals with a printed name and title beneath a handwritten signature in this block are signoff persons.

PATTERN 3 - Standalone signature block: A signature line or box with a printed name and title beneath it, appearing at the end of the main body of the document (not inside an annex or exhibit table).

CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Do NOT extract individuals who are merely listed in annexes, schedules, or tables as authorized persons for specific roles (e.g., authorized bank signatories, dealers, payment approvers), UNLESS they also appear in a signature block matching Pattern 1, 2, or 3 above.

FIELDS TO EXTRACT:

1. NAME
   Extract the full name exactly as printed below the signature.

2. DESIGNATION
   Extract the role/title printed below the name or next to the signature line.
   If no title is found anywhere, set "NA".

OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE:
{
  "Signoff_Persons": [
    {
      "Name": "John Smith",
      "Designation": "Director"
    },
    {
      "Name": "Jane Doe",
      "Designation": "NA"
    }
  ]
}
